From 80a3ce851df2abf1c74bd285f36d1877bb13a261 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 17:59:35 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] perf(sim): a field block stock builds in closed form, not by
 band fill

#633: the field engine took ~58 s (release) to BUILD a 120 mm block at
a 0.375 mm cell - the floorless block is meshed ten spans deep and the
BFS band fill sampled every cell along those walls - while its cuts
took milliseconds. A block's mesh-layer magnitude is now the box's
exact closed-form distance (field_box::AnalyticBox): SdfField::from_box
stores no bricks and mag_at answers unstored cells from the box,
clamped to cap. Build: 58 s -> 42 us; same cut cells (399/416).

Pinned by field_block_cost: a block stores no band at build; the
closed form reads the band-filled stock's sign everywhere within two
cells; a heavy-lane budget (120 mm block + drill under 2 s, release).

Fixes #633

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX
